Page 24 – Python Source Code (Part 2)
Member Registration and Display

This section registers new members and displays the registered member list.
def add_member():    name = input("Member name: ").strip()    class_name = input("Class/section: ").strip()    phone = input("Phone (optional): ").strip()    if not name:        print("Member name cannot be blank.")        return    with connect() as con:        con.execute("""            INSERT INTO members            (name, class_name, phone)            VALUES (?, ?, ?)        """, (name, class_name, phone))    print("Member registered successfully.")def view_members():    with connect() as con:        rows = con.execute("""            SELECT member_id, name, class_name, phone            FROM members            ORDER BY name        """).fetchall()    if not rows:        print("No members registered.")    else:        for row in rows:            print(row)



Explanation:
- add_member() collects the member's details.
- view_members() displays all registered members.
- SQLite automatically generates a unique Member ID.
- The member ID is used when issuing books.
