Page 26 – Python Source Code (Part 4)
View Issued Books and Main Menu
def view_issued_books():    with connect() as con:        rows = con.execute("""            SELECT t.transaction_id, b.title, m.name,                   t.issue_date, t.due_date, t.status            FROM transactions AS t            JOIN books AS b            ON t.book_id = b.book_id            JOIN members AS m            ON t.member_id = m.member_id            WHERE t.status = 'ISSUED'            ORDER BY t.due_date        """).fetchall()    if not rows:        print("There are no currently issued books.")    else:        for row in rows:            print(row)def show_menu():    print("\n========== LIBRARY MANAGEMENT SYSTEM ==========")    print("1. Add a book")    print("2. View all books")    print("3. Search for a book")    print("4. Register a member")    print("5. View members")



Explanation:

The view_issued_books() function displays the books that have not yet been returned.

The SQL JOIN command connects the Books, Members and Transactions tables to display the relevant information together.
